---
// Families and kids (#225, part of #210): one front door for young children.
// Birth to Three, Pre-K and Head Start, Starting Points, library story times.
// Babies and toddlers (#266): breastfeeding help (#572), baby pantries (#574),
// parent groups (#575) and home visits (#576). Not here until confirmed
// (#569): Help Me Grow's phone, the WVU Medicine lactation clinic, Right From
// The Start's local agency, Starting Points playgroup days, Scott's Run hours.
// Not yet here until confirmed: 4-H (#416), Early Head Start (#417),
// next year's Pre-K dates and summer meals (#418).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
export const page = { door: "family", topic: "family", label: "Families and kids", summary: "Babies, toddlers and preschool: Birth to Three, Pre-K, Head Start, child care, home visits, breastfeeding help, diapers, playgroups and story times" };
const all = loadDir('resources');
const r = (slug) => all.find((e) => e.slug === slug);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="Families and kids in Morgantown and Mon County: Birth to Three, Pre-K, playgroups" description="Help for families with babies, toddlers and preschoolers in Mon County: WV Birth to Three, Pre-K and Head Start, home visits while pregnant, free breastfeeding classes, baby pantries for diapers and formula, playgroups, story times and parent groups.">
  <h1>Help for families with young kids in Mon County</h1>
  <p class="lede">Worried about how your baby or toddler is growing? Call WV Birth to Three at <a href="tel:18663214728">1-866-321-4728</a>. Parents can call on their own, and there is no charge for the services in your child's plan.</p>

  <h2>Under 3: worried about how your child is growing</h2>
  <p>Birth to Three helps children under 3 who have a delay in how they move, talk, learn or get along, or who may be at risk of one. You do not need a doctor to send you.</p>
  {r('wv-birth-to-three-referral') && <ResourceCard r={r('wv-birth-to-three-referral')} showCost />}
  <p>Steps for each age, in one list: <a href={`${base}/life-events/child-delay-or-disability/`}>My child has a delay or disability</a>.</p>

  <h2>Ages 3 and 4: Pre-K and Head Start</h2>
  <p>The county schools run both, with one application. The dates for the 2027-28 school year are not posted yet. For 2026-27, applications sent from February 4 to April 16 all had an equal chance at a spot.</p>
  {r('mcs-prek-and-head-start') && <ResourceCard r={r('mcs-prek-and-head-start')} showCost />}

  <h2 id="home-visits">Help at home while pregnant or with a new baby</h2>
  {r('wvu-hapi-home-visiting') && <ResourceCard r={r('wvu-hapi-home-visiting')} />}
  {r('wv-home-visiting') && <ResourceCard r={r('wv-home-visiting')} />}

  <h2 id="feeding">Feeding your baby</h2>
  {r('monchd-wic-breastfeeding') && <ResourceCard r={r('monchd-wic-breastfeeding')} />}

  <h2 id="diapers">Diapers, wipes and formula</h2>
  <p>We have not found a diaper bank in Mon County. Two places give out baby items: Scott's Run Settlement House, by appointment, and the Starting Points baby pantry at The Shack, Wednesdays from 9 a.m. to noon, with items based on what is on hand.</p>
  {r('srsh-baby-pantry') && <ResourceCard r={r('srsh-baby-pantry')} />}

  <h2 id="child-care">Finding child care, and help paying for it</h2>
  <p>The state keeps one search for child care it licenses or registers. You can filter it to Monongalia County. To ask about providers near you and help with the cost, call the Child Care Resource Center in Morgantown.</p>
  {r('wv-child-care-provider-search') && <ResourceCard r={r('wv-child-care-provider-search')} />}
  {r('child-care-resource-center-morgantown') && <ResourceCard r={r('child-care-resource-center-morgantown')} showCost />}
  <p>Applied for help paying for child care? <a href={`${base}/after-you-apply/child-care/`}>After you apply for child care help</a> says what comes next.</p>

  <h2 id="playgroups">Playgroups, a baby pantry and more</h2>
  <p>Starting Points in Pursglove has free programs for parents and young children, including a playgroup for children under 3 and their parents.</p>
  {r('starting-points-family-programs') && <ResourceCard r={r('starting-points-family-programs')} />}

  <h2 id="story-times">Story times and baby play time at the library</h2>
  {r('mympls-story-times') && <ResourceCard r={r('mympls-story-times')} />}

  <h2 id="parent-groups">Meet other parents</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Starting Points: a playgroup for children under 3 with their parents, and a parent group with Happy School (above).</li>
    <li>The library: Read Baby Read and the Cheat Area Toddler Playgroup (above).</li>
    <li>WIC's free breastfeeding classes, open to anyone (above).</li>
  </ul>
  {r('ced-circle-of-parents') && <ResourceCard r={r('ced-circle-of-parents')} />}

  <h2 id="car-seats">Car seat checks</h2>
  <p>Two places in Morgantown check car seats by appointment. See <a href={`${base}/car-seat-checks/`}>Car seat checks</a>.</p>

  <h2>Also for families</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Short on food this month: <a href={`${base}/help/food/`}>Food help</a>.</li>
    <li>Help buying groceries each month: <a href={`${base}/snap/`}>Apply for SNAP</a>.</li>
    <li>Checkups, shots and dental visits: <a href={`${base}/staying-well/`}>Staying well</a>.</li>
    <li>A child with a disability at school: <a href={`${base}/disability-and-aging/#mcs-special-education`}>special education contacts</a>.</li>
    <li>Anything else: <a href="tel:211">call 211</a>, any hour.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="meta">Sources checked October 30, 2026. Call before you go, since hours and dates can change. Something out of date or missing? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
